From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: bridge: notify switchdev before a static FDB move

Moving a static FDB entry with bridge fdb replace updates fdb->dst before
notifying switchdev. The old destination therefore never receives a
delete. DSA can retain CPU-port address references after a move onto a
user port and skip programming the hardware on a later move back to a
foreign bridge port. The software and hardware FDB then disagree.

Notify the old destination before changing it, as the dynamic learning
path in br_fdb_update already does. Reproduced on YT9224 by moving a test
MAC from a DSA port to ap-mld0, back to DSA and to ap-mld0 again. Replaying
an explicit delete before each add restores correct CPU-port programming.

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>


From github.com/JiaY-shi/openwrt, branch flint4-support (cf069fb174),
target/linux/mediatek/patches-6.18/967-47-net-bridge-notify-old-port-on-static-fdb-moves.patch.
Hunks regenerated against GL's 6.12 YT922x driver.
---
--- a/net/bridge/br_fdb.c
+++ b/net/bridge/br_fdb.c
@@ -1120,6 +1120,7 @@
 			return -EEXIST;
 
 		if (READ_ONCE(fdb->dst) != source) {
+			br_switchdev_fdb_notify(br, fdb, RTM_DELNEIGH);
 			WRITE_ONCE(fdb->dst, source);
 			modified = true;
 		}
